# Optional non-secret overlay environment for the LOCAL Qwen3Guard pilot profile.
#
# Combine this file AFTER the base env file, never instead of it:
#
#   docker compose \
#     --env-file .secrets/compose.env \
#     --env-file .secrets/compose.pilot.env \
#     -f compose.yaml -f compose.pilot.yaml config
#
# Later --env-file entries win for duplicate keys.  This file intentionally
# contains NO generation/model settings, so the base values such as
# NASI_LEMAK_GENERATION_URL, NASI_LEMAK_GENERATION_MODEL,
# NASI_LEMAK_GENERATION_AUTH and NASI_LEMAK_GENERATION_ALLOW_INSECURE_HTTP are
# not overridden by accident.  The exact provider model ID and (for bearer auth)
# NASI_LEMAK_GENERATION_API_KEY must be supplied in the base env file only.
#
# This is the local-guard vertical.  Do NOT add any NASI_LEMAK_INPUT_GUARD_* or
# NASI_LEMAK_OUTPUT_GUARD_* hosted API settings here or combine this file with
# compose.api.yaml / compose.api-ca.yaml.  The overlay selects
# NASI_LEMAK_GUARD_BACKEND=qwen3guard-local and sets guarded mode itself; do not
# set either value again in this file.
#
# Only paths and non-secret tunables belong here.  Never put a password, a DSN
# containing a password, an application/operator key, a key digest or a model
# license value in this file, shell history, chat or Git.

# --- Read-only policy and model artifacts (host paths) ----------------------
# One operator-approved YAML policy file (see docs/policy.example.yaml for the
# exact accepted form).  Preserve each approved version under a new path.
PILOT_POLICY_FILE=/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/policy/2026-10-20.1.yaml

# Locally obtained, license-approved Qwen3Guard-Gen directory.  The operator
# must supply the complete config/tokenizer/safetensors bundle; nothing is
# downloaded by the image or at container start.  The same directory is mounted
# read-only at /models/qwen3guard-gen-0.6b and named to the application through
# NASI_LEMAK_QWEN3GUARD_MODEL_DIR.  Qwen3Guard-Stream is not supported (it needs
# remote code, which the product rejects).
PILOT_QWEN_GUARD_MODEL_DIR=/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/models/qwen3guard-gen-0.6b

# --- Optional validated guard settings (bare pass-throughs) -----------------
# Omitted entries keep the documented application defaults.  Thresholds are a
# categorical severity floor in [0.0, 0.5], not a calibrated probability: 0.5
# blocks Controversial and Unsafe verdicts.  workers * threads must not exceed
# the CPU count; the 4-vCPU guard box defaults to 2 workers x 2 threads.  The
# long-input budget is a per-call payload budget in 512..32768; it is never
# truncated and over-budget input fails closed.
NASI_LEMAK_QWEN3GUARD_INPUT_THRESHOLD=0.5
NASI_LEMAK_QWEN3GUARD_OUTPUT_THRESHOLD=0.5
# NASI_LEMAK_QWEN3GUARD_WORKERS=2
# NASI_LEMAK_QWEN3GUARD_THREADS=2
# NASI_LEMAK_QWEN3GUARD_LONG_INPUT=8192

# --- Provisional resource budget (not benchmarked) --------------------------
# Separate from the 512 MiB / 1 CPU lightweight default.  The adapter is
# CPU-only in this repository; no GPU support or performance claim is made.
GUARD_MEM_LIMIT=8g
GUARD_CPUS=4.0
GUARD_PIDS_LIMIT=512

# --- Distinct operator secret FILE paths ------------------------------------
# operator_key_digest: lowercase 64-hex SHA-256 digest of the operator key.
# This digest must differ from the chat application key digest.
# operator_audit_dsn: read-only reader-role PostgreSQL DSN.  It must differ
# from the runtime writer DSN in AUDIT_DSN_FILE.
#
# These are host files.  The container UID/GID 10001 must be able to read them;
# Compose local file-secret uid/gid/mode remapping is not claimed here.
OPERATOR_KEY_DIGEST_FILE=/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/.secrets/operator_key_digest
OPERATOR_AUDIT_DSN_FILE=/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/.secrets/operator_audit_dsn
